  "reason": "The top performer is config_014 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted) at 0.7250 accuracy, with config_036 (same but concat fusion) at 0.7207 and config_032 (resnet50, weighted) at 0.7131. The RNA encoder (scvi_n200) and image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) choices are well-supported. The remaining key uncertainty in the top-performing region is whether the transformer aggregation is truly necessary or whether a simpler avgpool aggregation could perform comparably. Config_033 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) is a direct single-variable ablation of the best config, testing only the aggregation choice. This is the highest-information experiment: if avgpool matches transformer, it confirms architectural robustness and frees remaining budget for other refinements; if it drops significantly, it confirms transformer is critical and we should lock in that choice. With 3 experiments left after this, resolving this uncertainty is essential before committing to final exploitation runs."
